  "body": "feat(ui): the Rotary Flow icon, panel hints and MCP surface pins\n\nStacked on #3999. Also fixes the Flow editor findings of the #4005\nreview (items 2, 3 and 4) on this branch, since this branch owns the\neditor file.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **Passes tab, stated axis** (#4005 review item 2): `stated_axis` was\n  discarded by the new arm - files and MCP could set it, the GUI could\n  not. It now binds through `rotary_stated_axis_editor` above the pose\n  trio. Pinned by\n  `the_stated_axis_arms_edits_applies_and_undoes_on_the_flow` (arm,\n  staged draft, Apply, one undo).\n- **Heights tab, retract hop** (#4005 review item 3): `retract_hop`\n  seeded `top + 1 mm`, and both its arguments here are the clearance\n  radius - the seeded retract cylinder sat ABOVE clearance. New\n  `retract_radius_hop` in `heights_page.rs`: the row is \"Retract\n  radius\", the seed sits 1 mm inside the clearance radius, and the hint\n  describes the cylinder, not a plane. Pinned by\n  `the_retract_hop_seeds_a_radius_below_the_clearance_radius` (toggle,\n  displayed readout `(= Z 44.000)` under the clearance's `(= Z\n  45.000)`, Apply, one undo).\n- **Passes tab, radial pose wording** (#4005 review item 4):\n  `axis_editor` words lead and max tilt off the surface normal, but\n  `rotary_flow_emit::cut_pose` measures them off the radial. The arm now\n  uses `rotary_axis_editor`, like the rotary twins.\n- **Guide hint**: the Passes tab says what the picked chains are for -\n  they span the band, pick them on the Geometry tab, a non-chain pick\n  refuses by name.\n- **Icon**: the `op-rotary-flow` PNG on the parent had drifted from its\n  SVG master, so `cargo xtask icons` re-rasterised it (the `icons\n  --check` gate breaches on the parent's tree); the flow lines are\n  drawn a touch steeper to read at 16 px. Original artwork, recorded in\n  `assets/ui/LICENSES.md` alongside the other original glyphs.\n- **MCP pins** (new `crates/app/tests/mcp_rotary_flow.rs`, one reason\n  for the top-level file: the multiaxis MCP binary is at 360 lines and\n  the 400-line law says split): `list_operation_types` lists Rotary\n  Flow, `add_operation` creates it, `edit_operation` edits the band\n  fields, a chain pick is accepted and a face or vertex pick is refused\n  by the `kind_door` chain-only arm.\n- **UI structural pins**: the Multi-axis dropdown lists and creates\n  Rotary Flow (`ribbon_accesskit.rs`); the Passes tab draws the axis\n  group, the band rows and the guide hint (`rotary_flow_page.rs`).\n\n## Readings\n\n- The review of #4005 (`pr-reviewer d9d71b6f`), items 2-4.\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/rotary_stated_axis.rs` (#2772's structural\n  harness) and `crates/app/tests/mcp_multiaxis_deburr.rs` (the MCP\n  surface pattern) were the models.\n- `rotary_stated.rs` already routes RotaryFlow through the stated-axis\n  resolver, and `kinds.rs` seeds it - the editor now matches both.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nBefore/after of the ribbon dropdown glyph and the Flow property panel,\nwith 4x crops, on the fork's `pr-screenshots` branch\n(`shots/rotary-flow-{before,after}-*.png`, commit `f2930e869`):\nhttps://github.com/FlamingFireCoding/Camcraft/tree/pr-screenshots/shots\nThese also cover review item 1 of #4005 - the reviewer's requested\nbefore/after of the Flow editor and icons.\n\n## Gate\n\n- `camcraft-ui` lib: 1654 passed, 0 failed, 8 ignored (the\n  release-lane snapshot set).\n- `camcraft-app --test mcp_rotary_flow`: 1 passed.\n- clippy `-p camcraft-ui -p camcraft-app --all-targets -D warnings`:\n  clean.\n- `cargo xtask icons --check`: 0 breaches.\n\nNot exercised: generation and posting of a GUI-authored Flow band (the\nkernel side is #4005's and #2826's); the screenshot harness itself is\nuncommitted, its outputs are the six PNGs.\n\nChangelog: the Rotary Flow band's stated rotation axis and radial\nretract are editable in the operation panel, and its icon renders in\nthe ribbon.\n\nFixes #2827\n",
